WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.790
The Jumanji franchise is apparently taking
action-comedy to... well, it's right there

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:05.480
in the title.

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:09.660
The third film in the series, Jumanji: The
Next Level, has screened for critics, and

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:13.260
while they're not yet allowed to pen formal
reviews, many of them have taken to social

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:14.900
media to offer their praise.

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:19.080
Singled out for heaping helpings of accolades
is Kevin Hart, who spent much of the sequel

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:20.480
channeling Danny Glover.

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:23.020
If that sounds confusing, here's a little
backstory.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:28.140
The 1995 classic Jumanji dealt with the plight
of two children who play a jungle-themed board

00:00:28.159 --> 00:00:32.439
game that unleashes its hazards on the real
world as they play and who soon discover that

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:34.600
it's possible to get physically sucked into
the game.

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:40.200
The 2017 sequel Jumanji: Welcome to the Jungle
expanded the original film's lore by morphing

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:41.640
Jumanji into a video game.

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:46.360
Four teens find themselves not only transported
into the game's world, but transformed into

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:51.230
its avatars: Dwayne Johnson's Dr. Smolder
Bravestone, Jack Black's Professor Sheldon

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:56.240
Oberon, Kevin Hart's Franklin "Mouse" Finbar,
and Karen Gillan's Ruby Roundhouse.

00:00:56.540 --> 00:01:00.879
Jumanji: The Next Level finds the teens forced
to once again jump back into the game along

00:01:00.879 --> 00:01:05.130
with one character's grandfather, played by
Danny Devito, and grandfather's friend, played

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:05.960
by Danny Glover.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:10.270
The two old folks are involuntarily brought
along for the ride and assigned the avatars

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:11.760
of Bravestone and Finbar.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:15.640
Critics who took to Twitter to offer up their
assessments of the flick were near-unanimous

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:20.190
in claiming that Jumanji: The Next Level is
absolutely a worthy sequel and Hart totally

00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:23.920
nailing the well-known mannerisms of Glover
was roundly considered to be a highlight.

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:26.320
"What in the Sam Hill?"

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.360
As Sean O'Connell of CinemaBlend wrote,

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:34.020
"[Jumanji: The Next Level] has some huge surprises
and introduces a LOT of story that's fun to

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:34.520
explore.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:36.280
The best reason to go back into the game?

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:38.420
[Kevin Hart] channeling Danny Glover.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:40.920
That joke kept making me laugh long and hard!"

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:44.100
TV personality Tara Hitchcock concurred, writing,

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:48.400
"Hard 2 top [Jack Black] as a teenage girl
in the last [Jumanji] film, but [Kevin Hart]

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:49.820
as Danny Glover DOES IT!

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:53.860
Omg I could listen 2 him tell me the backstory
of wild animals all day!"

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:57.480
Almost slipping through the cracks in all
of the adoration for Hart was the fact that

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:01.950
Johnson was tasked with being similarly convincing
as DeVito in the Rock's body, and he also

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:02.680
came through.

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:03.780
"Are we dead?"

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:06.120
Today Show correspondent Nikki Novak wrote,

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:10.759
"Here's what's next level about [Jumanji:
The Next Level] [Kevin Hart] as Danny Glover.

00:02:10.759 --> 00:02:12.160
The set pieces brilliant!

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:14.840
This time you really feel you are immersed
in a video game.

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:18.220
Danny DeVito charms and [The Rock] goes [over
the top] in channeling him.

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:19.300
What a blast!"

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:23.000
Other Twitter critics were there to dole out
praise to the entire cast.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:24.980
ComicBook.com's Brandon Davis wrote,

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:27.120
"[Jumanji: The Next Level] is hilarious.

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:30.620
It's impossible to pick one cast member who
stands out above the rest.

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:32.480
It has some unexpected heart, too.

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:32.980
Big time.

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:34.620
Everyone is so damn funny."

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:39.600
The overall response was perhaps best summed
up best by TV personality Maude Garrett, who

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:42.780
offered pretty much the highest praise any
sequel could ask for by saying,

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:47.740
"[Jumanji: The Next Level] does what few sequels
can do... make a movie that's just as good,

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:49.090
if not better than the first.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:53.319
They kept what was fun and built on it, with
hilarious changes that left me laughing out

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:54.120
loud often.

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:55.140
Worth seeing."

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:59.400
Fans will have to see if the rapturous response
to the flick holds up when the actual reviews

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:00.200
start coming in.

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:04.380
But so far, all signs point to Jumanji: The
Next Level being just as great a time at the

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:05.660
movies as Welcome to the Jungle.

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:08.300
The flick hits the big screen on December
13th.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:09.380
"I knew it!"

